// XFAIL: RT-454c: (RT-454's mechanism, with `Item =` written) `fn first<I: Iterator>(i: I) -> Option<I::Item>` called with `mk(&v)` returning `impl Iterator<Item = &'a i64>` is refused in the instance: "expected 'Option<{error}>', got 'Option<&i64>'" and, inside std, "'impl Iterator<Item = &'a i64>' has no associated type 'Item'"; rustc prints Some(1000) (0.30.2)
// Written from the re-review of g302bor2 (its forms t08 and o14), with
// nothing dropped. Since v0.30.1 at least (the same errors on v0.30.1 and
// the release build). The use-after-free side is rt_454d.
// EXPECT: Some(1000)
fn mk<'a>(v: &'a Vec<i64, Gpa>) -> impl Iterator<Item = &'a i64> {
    v.iter()
}

fn first<I: Iterator>(i: I) -> Option<I::Item> {
    let mut i = i;
    i.next()
}

fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let mut v: Vec<i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    v.push(1000);
    let r = first(mk(&v));
    println("{:?}", r);
}
